Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||09-15-2000||12:09 AM||||Loki, you might be lucky to have saved your money. You know of George Ryan? This is what he says about the Slalom Kit -<P>Naw - my terminal understeer was that stupid Ryane slolum front suspension I<BR>spent so much $ on - it has caused me so much grief that I finally have<BR>decided to quit wasting any more time and $ trying to make it handle. The<BR>early suspension that I had set up and handling well (remember when you<BR>first saw the car?) is going back under it.<P>G<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||09-15-2000||10:30 AM||||Who is George Ryan? I'd love to hear more about his endeavors with Ryane's slalom front end, or anybody else's for that matter. Is anybody running any of the Ryane components? Damn! That setup was supposed to be the basis for kicking some but next season. I can probably swing the Sport front end by September but it's a lousy time to have to drop the coin though. Maybe it's time to start looking for an '88  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Wannabe (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||KnightRyder31||09-15-2000||11:39 AM||||They must like the smell of burnt rice. I hate rice burner's!!!! Ricer's make me puke!||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||09-15-2000||03:29 PM||||I received notice of ryane's dropping the Fiero line about a year ago. They said if sales don't improve, the fiero stuff will no longer be produced. I guess sales didn't improve. Hey Archie, here's another company for you to purchase! <P>I had the Ryane coil-overs on the rear of my Lambo replica, and they were great, but I could have bought all the parts seperately and made the simple top mount myself and saved a lot of money. In fact thats what I did for the Ferrari I'm working on.<P>Anyway, I'll be sad to see them go.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierov8||09-15-2000||04:41 PM||||Yeah -- I'll be very sad to see them go.<P>Now where will us Fiero fanatics turn for insanely priced parts, extremely long delays, and poor post-sales service?<P>Was going to purchase a Slalom front end and the larger brake kit that goes with it -- then totalled up the cost -&gt; $4800!!!Yikes!!!!!!!!!!!<P>And I have talked with George Ryan -- he's the maintainer for the FieroRacingList and an avid autocrosser/Fiero driver.  From what he's told me, he's been putzing with the Slalom suspension for two seasons and still isn't dialed in.  And apparently Mr. Armstrong hasn't been too helpful post-sale.  Pretty nice for a $2400 investment, don't you think?<P>My personal experience with Mr. Armstrong has been relatively sour -- parts received with no instructions, eternal waits for quotes (_still_ waiting for a quote on doing a semi-custom coilover -- guess that ain't happening).<P>About the only good that could come of this is for someone to purchase his jigs, drawings, etc. and redesign where necessary and offer at a reasonable price.<P>-jeff d<BR>Fort Worth, TX<BR>'86 Emod autocrosser<p>[This message has been edited by fierov8 (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||13
Z||000008||TwisT||09-15-2000||08:17 PM||||Guys,  I'm yet another Fiero owner disappointed in Ryane's move,  though I completely understand his position.  <P>I've been waiting for the day to come when I had some extra cash to purchase coil-overs and spindles from him...  now it looks as if I will be looking for alternatives.  SHUCKS...  Ryane has had the PRIME hardware for our Fiero's for the longest time;  sure hope we don't have to settle for some "brand-X" equipment!<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000009||Wannabe||09-16-2000||09:32 AM||||Has anyone ever looked at adapting the C4 Corvette control arms and spindles to the Fiero subframe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">?||||reg||1
Z||000010||dman||09-16-2000||06:08 PM||||Hello everyone. Hey wannabe, the following webpage is of a Ferrari Testarossa replica based on a fiero. The builder used Corvette spindles and brakes for the front and Cadillac STS spindles and brakes for the rear. The rear suspension is highly customized however since it seems he built custom length arms and axles to get a wide track suspension. So chances are it may take a little bit of work to get something simliar to work on a stock Fiero.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Street/8044/brakepage1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Street/8044/brakepage1.html</A> <P>I stumbled across that web page earlier this year but I've never contacted the author of that site so I don't know more than whats described on those pages.<P>||||reg||1
